<h2>CSS groups</h2>
<p>Drupal orders CSS by group. A stylesheet is assigned to a group by its file name: <code>*.layout.css</code>, <code>*.component.css</code>, <code>*.state.css</code> and <code>*.theme.css</code>. Everything else is <code>base</code>. The group suffix is removed from the library name, so <code>css/card.component.css</code> and <code>css/card.ts</code> share the library <code>css__card</code>.</p>

{% embed aside with { type: 'caution', title: 'Known issue in production builds' } %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>With Vite 8, a production build of <code>css/demo.component.css</code> produced <code>demo.[hash].css</code> in the dist root. The resulting library was <code>demo</code> in group <code>base</code> instead of <code>css__demo</code> in group <code>component</code>. The dev server uses the source file names and is not affected.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

<h2>Dev vs. build</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Dev:</strong> all assets are external URLs pointing to the Vite dev server, plus a <code>vite</code> library that loads <code>/@vite/client</code> for HMR.</li>
  <li><strong>Build:</strong> hashed files in <code>dist/</code>, scripts as <code>type: module</code>, never preprocessed or aggregated by Drupal.</li>
</ul>
